    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7023",
      "problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8,\n\\qquad\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D}  3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(8+(-5)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
